{"classification":"mathematical-inconsistent-pseudometric-notation","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0367","math_ordinal":48,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-COMPLETE-CORPUS-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The proof concerns rho_tau throughout, and tau is a one-argument functional; the unsubscripted rho and two-argument tau(u,v) contradict the defining formula immediately above.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt2a5.tex:96-97","source_normalized_sha256":"902d9fa79c51cdac9675c86562b0497c4c83f21d0ddf98b09e4e9edeee785c30","source_text":"\\rho(v,u)=\\tau(v-u)=\\tau(-1(u-v))\\le\\tau(u,v)=\\rho_{\\tau}(u,v)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt2a5.tex:95-96","target_normalized_sha256":"7d6970f5156daf569a733eb0e53163d9ab5d09c4bd9f362cb36831397de8e05c","target_text":"\\rho_{\\tau}(v,u)=\\tau(v-u)=\\tau(-1(u-v))\\le\\tau(u-v)=\\rho_{\\tau}(u,v)","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-APP-2A5"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-functional-arity","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0368","math_ordinal":188,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-COMPLETE-CORPUS-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Each tau_i is an F-seminorm on U, not a two-argument function; the Cauchy criterion in 2A5G uses tau_i(u-v).","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt2a5.tex:287","source_normalized_sha256":"9e341bc354ff2ba299e9f18c725e29b5de00551d2c7f4efbd7e8e5c4407e4389","source_text":"\\tau_i(u,v)<\\bover{\\epsilon}2","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt2a5.tex:290","target_normalized_sha256":"ff615cacc1748d9960de359a7406dd80b424f7524a2c12dd51ef11a6e335b783","target_text":"\\tau_i(u-v)<\\bover{\\epsilon}2","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-APP-2A5"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-sequence-index","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0369","math_ordinal":226,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-COMPLETE-CORPUS-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The quantified tail statement is for every n greater than or equal to m; its norm must therefore use u_n, not the fixed threshold term u_m.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt2a5.tex:320","source_normalized_sha256":"986cca6a212022556ce9fd1dc19bb3caa0d005b6badd222824f383007c021db9","source_text":"\\|u_m-u\\|<\\epsilon","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt2a5.tex:325","target_normalized_sha256":"7486096b819e0838c93f235374780b3c03932cfd07298985ead818e54f0b92c8","target_text":"\\|u_n-u\\|<\\epsilon","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-APP-2A5"}
